  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If the ebucore:hasMimeType value of an 'fcr:metadata' resource has an invalid mimetype string, such as \"audio/3gpp, video/3gpp\", Fedora will throw a 500 error when requesting the binary content:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "curl -X GET ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://host/binary"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://host/binary",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: Error parsing media type 'audio/3gpp, video/3gpp'",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "at org.glassfish.jersey.message.internal.MediaTypeProvider.fromString(MediaTypeProvider.java:92)",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "at org.glassfish.jersey.message.internal.MediaTypeProvider.fromString(MediaTypeProvider.java:60)",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "at javax.ws.rs.core.MediaType.valueOf(MediaType.java:179)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "To reproduce:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "1) Create a binary resource.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "2) Modify the ebucore:hasMimeType value so that it contains two mimetype strings separated by a comma.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "3) Try to GET the binary.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This is a data issue caused by a client PATCHing the hasMimeType value with an invalid 'mimetype'.  It's fairly easily avoided and it's readily fixed by correcting the value.  ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "That said, it may be worth considering performing a check on the mimetype value and serving the bytes with a generic application/octet-stream content type when an invalid mimetype is detected.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
